I open the front door.
The shopping bag in my hand is heavy.
I walk slowly up the stairs.
On the second floor, a door opens.
My neighbour Sabine steps out.
Her small dog Bruno runs immediately to me.
"Hello, Maya!" Sabine says cheerfully.
"Hello, Sabine," I answer.
"Are you going for a walk?" I ask.
Sabine nods.
"Yes, the weather is so beautiful today," she explains.
I pet Bruno.
His fur is very soft.
"Are you coming from the office?" Sabine asks.
"Yes, I am finally done with work for the day now," I say.
"Then I wish you a nice evening," she says.
"Thank you, you too!" I reply.
Sabine and Bruno go down the stairs.
I continue upstairs to my flat.
